---
const docs = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_DOCS_URL || 'https://klicksea-docs.vercel.app';
const repo = 'https://github.com/techsavvyash/klicksea';
const download = repo + '/releases/download/v0.1.0-preview.1/KlickSea-0.1.0-preview-universal.dmg';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>KlickSea — A little clarity, right on your screen</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A quiet macOS companion. Capture what you're looking at, ask out loud, and hear a useful answer with Codex or Claude." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="KlickSea — Your screen. A little clearer." /><meta property="og:description" content="A voice-first macOS screen companion. Source available, built to stay out of your way." />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f5ef" /><link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" />
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="nav wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="KlickSea home"><img src="/icon.png" alt="" width="40" height="40" />KlickSea</a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href={docs}>Docs</a><a class="nav-github" href={repo}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>A quiet companion for your Mac</div>
      <h1>Your screen.<br /><em>A little clearer.</em></h1>
      <p class="intro">A shortcut. A question. A little help.<br />KlickSea sees what you’re looking at and talks it through with you.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="primary" href={download}>Download the preview DMG <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="secondary" href="#demo">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <p class="availability">macOS 15+ · Apple silicon + Intel · Preview is not notarized</p>
      <div class="scene" aria-label="Illustration of the voice companion over a sample work screen">
        <div class="sample-window"><div class="window-top"><div class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>northstar / launch notes</span><span class="sample-tag">Sample screen</span></div>
          <div class="sample-content"><aside><b>N /</b><span class="selected">Launch notes</span><span>Decisions</span><span>Ideas</span><span>Archive</span></aside>
            <article><span class="small-label">A little progress, every day</span><h2>Ready for the next step.</h2><p>There’s a lot on your screen.<br />You don’t have to untangle it alone.</p><div class="check"><span>✓</span> First build is working</div><div class="check"><span>✓</span> Voice and capture connected</div><div class="check pending"><span>○</span> Share with the team</div></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <img class="companion" src="/companion.png" width="580" height="108" alt="KlickSea’s native floating bar with waveform, microphone, capture, stop, and settings controls" />
        <span class="scene-caption">A sample screen, with the real native companion bar.</span>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="how-it-works" class="how wrap">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Less switching. More understanding.</span><h2>Keep your eyes on your work.</h2></div>
      <div class="steps"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Bring it into focus.</h3><p>Press <kbd>⌃</kbd> <kbd>⇧</kbd> <kbd>4</kbd> to capture the display under your pointer. Or record a short clip with <kbd>⌃ ⇧ 5</kbd>.</p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Say what you need.</h3><p>Ask about an error, a confusing page, or your next step. Pause briefly and KlickSea sends your question with the capture.</p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Hear a useful answer.</h3><p>Your selected agent explains what it sees. The bar disappears when you’re done, leaving your desktop to you.</p></article></div>
    </section>
    <section class="voice wrap"><div><span class="eyebrow">Your companion. Your choice.</span><h2>A familiar agent.<br />A voice that feels right.</h2></div><div class="voice-copy"><p>Use your existing Codex CLI login, or connect Claude with an Anthropic API key. Choose an installed macOS voice and a speaking speed that suits you.</p><p class="fine">Claude API usage is billed separately. Claude subscription reuse is not currently offered. Provider availability and usage limits apply.</p><a href={docs + '/providers'}>Set up your provider <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section id="demo" class="demo wrap"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">See the flow</span><h2>From “what’s going on?”<br />to “got it.”</h2></div>
      <div class="demo-content" data-demo-slot>
        <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/demo-poster.jpg" aria-label="KlickSea working demo: live capture and Codex answer with a scripted question">
          <source src="/demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <track kind="captions" src="/demo.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default />
          <p>Your browser does not support video. <a href="/demo.mp4">Download the demo.</a></p>
        </video>
        <div class="demo-note"><p><strong>Real capture. Real Codex response. Native spoken playback.</strong><br />This 37-second recording uses a scripted question on a clean sample screen. It does not demonstrate human microphone input.</p>
          <details><summary>Read the transcript</summary><p><strong>Question:</strong> What is blocking this launch, and what should I fix first?</p><p><strong>Answer:</strong> The checklist says trusted downloads are blocked because the app still needs a Developer ID Application certificate and notarization. Fix signing and notarization first, then test the downloaded app on another Mac before public release. The native build and documentation are marked complete.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="privacy wrap"><span class="eyebrow">A companion, on your terms.</span><h2>Only when you ask.</h2><div class="privacy-grid"><p>Captures start when you invoke a shortcut or control. Dictation runs on this Mac when your language supports it. KlickSea doesn’t continuously watch your desktop.</p><p>Your captured images and transcribed question go to the provider you select. KlickSea doesn’t send microphone audio to that provider. No KlickSea analytics or cloud conversation store.</p></div><a href={docs + '/privacy'}>Read how your data is handled <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
    <section class="closing wrap"><img src="/icon.png" alt="" width="56" height="56" /><h2>A little help.<br />Right where you are.</h2><p>Early, open, and getting better. Install the preview directly.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href={download}>Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="secondary" href={repo + '/releases'}>Follow releases</a></div><p class="fine">Preview uses a local development signature; macOS may require Open Anyway.<br />Developer ID signing and notarization are pending. See <a href={docs + '/getting-started'}>installation instructions</a>.</p></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/icon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" />KlickSea</a><span>Built by <a href="https://github.com/techsavvyash">techsavvyash</a></span><div><a href={docs + '/testing'}>Testing status</a><a href={docs}>Documentation</a><a href={repo}>Source</a></div></footer>
</body>
</html>
<style>
